## What to watch
- Reaction asymmetry: net news tone into the print is {{ "%+.2f" | format(earnings_tone) }}; a beat against negative tone has more room to rerate than a beat already priced in by positive tone.
- Index spillover: check the correlation of reporters to `{{ anchor }}` above. A high recent correlation means the print moves the index.
- Rates sensitivity: the 10Y move this week is {{ y10_move }}. Long-duration names react more to yields than to the earnings number itself.
